my name is kaylee i have a youtube  channel called the dolls in the rain and  i restore american girl dolls i'm going  to walk you through how i restore a  1990s felicity american girl doll  felicity merriman is one of american  girls six original historical characters  originally this doll would have sold for  around a hundred dollars but in its  current state it is worth about 55  after i restore her she'll probably be  worth around 200  felicity's biggest problems are  definitely her missing arm she has nail  polish on all of her hands and feet her  hair is very messy and the face paint is  faded  [Music]  so the first thing i'm doing is taking  off felicity's head i'm doing this by  untying her next ring i'm using a sewing  pin to help get the knot undone  [Music]  then once it's untied i'm just pulling  off her head  [Music]  now that her head is de-attached i'm  removing all of her stuffing i'm just  pulling it out by hand and collecting it  in a pile so i can use it again later on  [Music]  now that felicity is unstuffed i'm going  to take off her limbs so i'm just  untying these and again i'm using a  sewing pin to help undo the knots  now i have felicity's limbs de-attached  and next i'll be removing the tension  cups from inside of her arms and legs to  do this i'm putting her limbs into a  ziploc bag and boiling water in a kettle  i want the water to be boiling hot so  the vinyl melts  once the water is boiled i'm putting the  ziploc bag into the water and leaving it  there for about a minute this is going  to heat up the limbs so i can remove the  tension cups without cracking the limbs  now that the limbs are heated up i'm  using a pair of needle nose pliers to  pull the tension cups out  next i'm going to be cleaning felicity  felicity has nail polish on her  fingernails and her toenails american  girl dolls should not have nail polish  so obviously her previous owner has  painted them  [Music]  to do this i'm using non-acetone nail  polish remover it's very important to  use non-acetone nail polish remover as  acetone can damage vinyl  all i'm doing is putting the nail polish  remover onto a cotton ball and rubbing  the nail polish off  once i have most of it off i'm using a  fine q-tip to get into the crevices of  the nails  [Music]  now that all of the nail polish is off  i'm using a magic eraser to clean the  rest of her skin  over time american girl dolls can get  very dirty you can see this when they  are shiny it's just a collection of  grease and sometimes the oil from your  hands  i'm also using a magic eraser on her  face but i'm being very careful not to  scrub too hard on her lips and eyebrows  because this can remove the paint  [Music]  now that felicity is clean i'm going to  restring her  [Music]  now that all of her limbs are attached  to her body i am re-stuffing felicity  [Music]  once i have all of the stuffing back in  i reattach felicity's head i just put it  back into the opening and tie the string  tight  [Music]  now i'm going to begin fixing felicity's  hair which is one of the hardest parts  of restoring an old doll her hair is  very frizzy and matted  i use a spray bottle and a wired hair  brush to help get all of the knots out  when i'm brushing doll hair i always  start from the bottom of the wig and  then work my way upwards so i'm not  dragging down the knots to the bottom of  the hair  next i'll be straightening felicity's  hair i'm doing this to remove the frizz  i'm making sure her hair is very wet as  using a straightener on dry american  girl doll hair can burn it  i finished straightening all of  felicity's hair and usually i would stop  there but felicity has pin curls at the  front of her head so i need to re-curl  those  i've straightened each of the three pin  curls and i'm going to be using a straw  and boiling water to get them back to  their original shape  i'm tying each little curl around a  plastic straw and securing it in place  with a bobby pin  [Music]  now i'm dipping the side of her head  into boiling water  i'm leaving it there for about 30  seconds  then i'm taking her head back out and  leaving her to dry  next i'm just removing the plastic  straws and her curls are back  [Music]  overall felicity's face paint has  definitely faded over time  her lips are faded her teeth are faded  her cheeks are faded and there is some  damage to her eyebrows  i'm using watercolors to paint  felicity's face i think it gives the  dolls a really natural look especially  with the older dolls that didn't have as  dramatic makeup as the newer dolls have  i'm using a very fine paint brush and  tracing over the lips that were already  there  i do this in one thin layer at a time  and then i blot it with a tissue  i'm happy with the shape of her lips i  can move on to the cheeks i'm using a  slightly bigger paintbrush here  i always leave it slightly lighter than  i would like because it dries dark  [Music]  i'm using some white acrylic craft paint  and very carefully filling in the teeth  [Music]  now that her teeth are done my last step  is to fill in her eyebrows  now that felicity is finished i've tied  her hair into her original hairstyle  with a little white ribbon in the back i  put her in this purple dress this is  from a newer edition of felicity now she  is ready to go on to her next owner and  be loved once again  [Music]
 

